Remove reflection from filters and swagger.

Code generators provide `IOperationDesciptor` implementations for all gRPC operations.
ServiceModel.Grpc.DesignTime generates c# code.
ServiceModel.Grpc.Emit generates implementation on-fly.

`IOperationDesciptor` is not a part of public API, and is designed for internal use only.

```c#
namespace ServiceModel.Grpc.Internal;

/// <summary>
/// This API supports ServiceModel.Grpc infrastructure and is not intended to be used directly from your code.
/// This API may change or be removed in future releases.
/// </summary>

public interface IOperationDescriptor
{
    MethodInfo GetContractMethod();

    bool IsAsync();

    int[] GetRequestHeaderParameters();

    int[] GetRequestParameters();

    IMessageAccessor GetRequestAccessor();

    IStreamAccessor? GetRequestStreamAccessor();

    IMessageAccessor GetResponseAccessor();

    IStreamAccessor? GetResponseStreamAccessor();
}

public interface IMessageAccessor
{
    string[] Names { get; }

    object CreateNew();

    Type GetValueType(int property);

    Type GetInstanceType();

    object? GetValue(object message, int property);

    void SetValue(object message, int property, object? value);
}

public interface IStreamAccessor
{
    void Validate(object stream);

    object CreateEmpty();

    Type GetInstanceType();
}
```

Proposes adding @StrikerRUS back to `CODEOWNERS`, to be automatically added as a reviewer on PRs.

@StrikerRUS since #5998, we've stopped having specialization in the `CODEOWNERS` file (no more "these people are R reviewers", "these people are Python reviewers", etc.) and switched to just having everyone added to every PR by default. That more closely matched the current state of the project and abilities/interests of the reviewers.

If you don't want to be added as a reviewer on every PR by default let me know, and we can close this.

